+The picker groups review requests by repository. Press `/` to filter by repo, title, author, or label; `j`/`k` to move; `Enter` to open; `o` to open the selected PR in a browser; or `r` to refresh. The list also refreshes itself every two minutes, keeping your place. Press `Space` to select PRs, `a` to select all PRs shown by the filter, and `d` to download the selected tours before opening them. With no selection, `d` downloads the highlighted tour. Downloads run one at a time and show progress in the picker; completed tours are cached for later opening. On a wide terminal, the preview shows the description, changed files, checks, review decision, and whether a local tour or drafts already exist.
 
 For a PR, Guided Review fetches metadata, the diff, and existing review threads through `gh`. It checks out the PR head in a detached worktree under `~/.guided-review/worktrees/`. Your own working checkout is left alone. If the current repository is not the PR's repository, it uses a cached clone under `~/.guided-review/repos/`.
 
